{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115967","id":3255514968,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7CCzdY","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115967","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115967.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115967.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115967","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115967/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115967/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115967/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/dbb554f9733e2cd8fb72ded5ceec092bb66a6536","number":115967,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"GDScript: Fix separated getter/setter return value and parameter conversions","user":{"login":"Hrothdel","id":32814943,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODE0OTQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32814943?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hrothdel","html_url":"https://github.com/Hrothdel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hrothdel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hrothdel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hrothdel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hrothdel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hrothdel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hrothdel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hrothdel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hrothdel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hrothdel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #91689\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes problems and inconsistencies with getters or setters defined by separate functions, on typed properties. The getter side of this is more involved.\r\n\r\nTo ensure the getter function result is automatically converted to the property type, without affecting the function itself (as it may have other uses), the compiler now generates new wrapper function for each such getter that needs a conversion. The wrapper just calls the assigned function and converts the results before returning it. The analyzer checks for getter functions that need to have their results converted, marks this using the new `VariableNode::use_getter_conversion` field. The compiler then checks this field and only generates wrappers when this is set.\r\n\r\nExample script:\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar prop_mismatched_getter: int: get = return_float\r\nvar prop_validated_getter: int: get = return_int\r\n\r\nfunc return_float():\r\n\treturn 1.0\r\n\r\nfunc return_int() -> int:\r\n\treturn 1\r\n\r\nfunc _run() -> void:\r\n\tvar target: int = prop_mismatched_getter\r\n\ttarget = prop_validated_getter\r\n```\r\n\r\nBytecode (before):\r\n```\r\nFunction return_float()\r\n 0: line 5: \treturn 1.0\r\n 2: return const(1.0)\r\n 4: == END ==\r\n\r\nFunction return_int()\r\n 0: line 8: \treturn 1\r\n 2: return const(1)\r\n 4: == END ==\r\n\r\nFunction _run()\r\n 0: line 11: \tvar target: int = prop_mismatched_getter\r\n 2: call-ret stack(4) = self.return_float()\r\n 8: assign stack(3) = stack(4)\r\n 11: line 12: \ttarget = prop_validated_getter\r\n 13: call-ret stack(4) = self.return_int()\r\n 19: assign stack(3) = stack(4)\r\n 22: == END ==\r\n```\r\n\r\nBytecode (after):\r\n```\r\nFunction @prop_mismatched_getter_getter()\r\n 0: line 1: var prop_mismatched_getter: int: get = return_float\r\n 2: call-ret stack(4) = self.return_float()\r\n 8: assign typed builtin (int) stack(3) = stack(4)\r\n 12: return stack(3)\r\n 14: == END ==\r\n\r\nFunction return_float()\r\n 0: line 5: \treturn 1.0\r\n 2: return const(1.0)\r\n 4: == END ==\r\n\r\nFunction return_int()\r\n 0: line 8: \treturn 1\r\n 2: return const(1)\r\n 4: == END ==\r\n\r\nFunction _run()\r\n 0: line 11: \tvar target: int = prop_mismatched_getter\r\n 2: call-ret stack(4) = self.@prop_mismatched_getter_getter()\r\n 8: assign stack(3) = stack(4)\r\n 11: line 12: \ttarget = prop_validated_getter\r\n 13: call-ret stack(4) = self.return_int()\r\n 19: assign stack(3) = stack(4)\r\n 22: == END ==\r\n```\r\n\r\nNote that matching typed functions don't get these wrappers (like `return_int` for `prop_validated_getter` from the example), minimizing overhead.\r\n\r\nOn the setter side, this fixes a inconsistency with converting the passed parameter to the property type at different points depending on how the setter was called.\r\n\r\nExample script:\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar prop_weak_setter: int:\r\n\tset = weak_setter\r\n\r\nfunc weak_setter(value):\r\n\tprop_weak_setter = value\r\n\tprints(var_to_str(value), var_to_str(prop_weak_setter))\r\n\r\nfunc _run() -> void:\r\n\tvar t: Variant = 1.0\r\n\tprop_weak_setter = t        # 1.0 1\r\n\tset(\"prop_weak_setter\", t)  # 1 1\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe `GDScript::set()` and `GDScript::_set()` methods performed this conversion regardless of whether the property had a setter or not. I just moved that conversion logic to the branch for direct access without a setter.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","la